linkpage — third-party notices
==============================

linkpage itself is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

This file covers the third-party material vendored into the renderer's source: the artwork in
`packages/renderer/src/icons.ts` and the weekday abbreviations in
`packages/renderer/src/locale.ts`. The renderer declares no dependencies (SPEC.md §5.1), so it
cannot import an icon library or a locale library — whatever it uses is copied into its source,
and this file is where those copies are attributed.

Two consequences worth stating plainly, because they are the reason these particular sources
were chosen (SPEC.md §2.4, §2.5):

  * **Font Awesome Free was specifically avoided.** Its CC BY 4.0 licence attaches an
    attribution obligation that would follow every page linkpage exports, onto every site
    those pages are published to. Nothing an owner exports from this tool carries an
    attribution requirement.

  * **Nothing below requires attribution in an exported `index.html`.** ISC, MIT and the
    Unicode licence ask that their notice accompany copies of *the software*, which this file
    provides for this repository; CC0 asks for nothing. The exported page is the owner's,
    outright.


