Simple Icons — social brand marks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

https://simpleicons.org
https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons
Vendored from simple-icons 16.28.0.

Marks used: instagram, facebook, x, tiktok, youtube, whatsapp, pinterest, threads, bluesky,
mastodon. Each was checked to be under the collection's default CC0 licence rather than a
per-icon exception.

Simple Icons is released under CC0 1.0 Universal:

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

CC0 waives copyright. It does not waive trademark, and paragraph 4(a) of the deed says so
explicitly. A brand mark used to link to that brand's own page is nominative use — it
identifies the destination and claims nothing else — which is precisely and only what these
marks do here.

LinkedIn is deliberately absent: Simple Icons removed the mark at LinkedIn's request. A
LinkedIn URL in a project still renders, with the generic link glyph, by the same mechanism
that carries any platform the set does not name (SPEC.md §4.4).


