Unicode CLDR — weekday abbreviations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

https://cldr.unicode.org
https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr
Vendored from Unicode CLDR 48.

The seven weekday abbreviations for each language in `packages/renderer/src/locale.ts` are
CLDR's `format`/`abbreviated` weekday names, extracted once and frozen into the source. They
are the same data `Intl.DateTimeFormat` would return; what SPEC.md §2.5 rules out is reading
them at render time from whichever ICU build happens to be running, because that would make the
exported bytes depend on the host rather than on the project (§6.7) and could make the owner's
preview differ from their file (§5.2).

**The word for a closed day is NOT from CLDR.** There is no locale database of the word a shop
puts on its door; that one string per language is hand-authored in this repository and is
governed by §2.5's growth rule, not by anything below. Corrections from speakers are welcome —
see CONTRIBUTING.md.

